### What will I learn?
- What a **NAT** actually is once you stop fearing it -- a box on your router that rewrites the source address and port of every packet on the way out, and remembers the swap so replies find their way home;
- Why two machines _both_ behind NAT cannot simply dial each other, even though either one can reach a public server fine;
- How **STUN** lets a machine ask \

